## Event scope

{{#if ingest}}This listener fires only from DIMSE C-STORE. `CStoreService` dispatches
ingest events at `CStoreService.java:364` and `CStoreService.java:382`.
DICOMweb STOW does not invoke it. The bean is consumed as
`List<StorageIngestEventListener>` by `CStoreService`.
{{/if}}{{#if retrieve}}This listener fires only from DICOMweb retrieval. `DicomwebRetrieveService`
dispatches retrieve events at `DicomwebRetrieveService.java:369` and
`DicomwebRetrieveService.java:382`. DIMSE C-MOVE does not invoke it. The bean is
consumed as `List<StorageRetrieveEventListener>` by `DicomwebRetrieveService`.
{{/if}}
## Configuration

Add this to the host `application.yml` (the tool never edits it):

```yaml
app:
  {{configFamily}}:
    {{id}}:
      # set enabled: true to activate
      enabled: false
```

{{#if ingest}}
> **Callback safety:** `CStoreService` dispatches ingest events with
> `listeners.forEach` at `CStoreService.java:364` and
> `CStoreService.java:382`; the loop has no per-listener exception isolation.
> A throwing listener aborts the remaining listeners, and a success callback
> exception can turn a successful C-STORE into a failure
> (`CStoreService.java:233-248`). This generated callback catches and logs
> `RuntimeException` and never rethrows.
{{/if}}{{#if retrieve}}
> **Callback safety:** `DicomwebRetrieveService` dispatches retrieve events
> with `retrieveEventListeners.forEach` at
> `DicomwebRetrieveService.java:369` and `DicomwebRetrieveService.java:382`;
> the loop has no per-listener exception isolation, so a throwing listener
> aborts the remaining listeners. This generated callback catches and logs
> `RuntimeException` and never rethrows.
{{/if}}
## Build

### Standalone mode

When `../../pom.xml` is absent, Maven resolves the parent from the local
repository. Install the pinned parent and SDK once from a dicoogle-next
checkout:

```bash
cd backend
./mvnw -B -ntp -N install
./mvnw -B -ntp -pl dicoogle-next-sdk -am install
```

Then build this module:

```bash
mvn -B -ntp spotless:check test
```

### In-repo mode

To build in place under `backend/plugins/{{artifactId}}`, add the module to
`backend/pom.xml` and add the dependency to `backend/dicoogle-next/pom.xml`.
The parent is then resolved from `../../pom.xml`. The tool never edits those
files.

```bash
cd backend
./mvnw -B -ntp -pl plugins/{{artifactId}} -am spotless:check test
```

